superlu_dist
------------------------------------------
SuperLU_DIST contains a set of subroutines to solve a sparse linear system
A*X=B. It uses Gaussian elimination with static pivoting (GESP). Static
pivoting is a technique that combines the numerical stability of partial
pivoting with the scalability of Cholesky (no pivoting), to run accurately and
efficiently on large numbers of processors.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgomp1-14.4.0-1
  liblapack0-3.12.0-1
  libmetis0-5.2.1-1
  libopenmpi40-4.1.6-1
  libptscotch7.0-7.0.18-1bl2
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  libsuperlu_dist-devel-9.3.2-1bl2
  libsuperlu_dist9-9.3.2-1bl2
  pkg-config-3.0.11-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.13-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gcc-fortran-14.4.0-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  liblapack-devel-3.12.0-1
  libmetis-devel-5.2.1-1
  libopenmpi-devel-4.1.6-1
  libscotch-devel-7.0.18-1bl2
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/xiaoyeli/superlu_dist

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/xiaoyeli/superlu_dist/archive/refs/tags/v9.3.2.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack superlu_dist-9.3.2-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./superlu_dist-9.3.2-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/superlu_dist-9.3.2-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/superlu_dist-9.3.2-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libsuperlu_dist9-9.3.2-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libsuperlu_dist-devel-9.3.2-X.tar.xz

